.TH "GYRO" "1" "Nov 2026" "Gyro Hosting" "gyro manual"

.SH NAME
gyro-service-resize-option-list - Products this service can be upgraded to, with prices


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBgyro service resize-option list  [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Products this service can be upgraded to, with prices

.PP
Prepaid services answer \fBbilling: prepaid\fR; each option has \fBplan\fR, \fBcurrent\fR and one \fBhourly\fR price with \fBmonthly_cap\fR\&. \fBData safety (Gyro Cloud Istanbul, tr-ist-1)\fP: a plan change keeps the disk and all its data, the IP addresses, additional disks and snapshots. The root disk is enlarged in place and the file system is extended automatically; a disk never shrinks, so a plan with a smaller disk is refused with 409 \fBdisk_shrink\fR (also in \fBdry_run\fR; resize-options marks such plans \fBallowed: false\fR). Bigger CPU/RAM is applied live when the hypervisor allows it, otherwise the server is shut down cleanly and started again (measured: 1-2 -> 2-4 restarted, about 12 seconds without SSH; 2-4 -> 4-8 live, no restart). While the server has snapshots the disk cannot grow: 409 \fBresize_refused\fR (delete the snapshots first). The answer carries \fBdata_preserved: true\fR, \fBdisk: grows_only\fR, \fBrestart: if_needed\fR\&. Only a rebuild (\fBPOST /cloud/servers/{id}/actions/rebuild\fR, needs \fBconfirm: true\fR) erases data: the disk, additional disks and snapshots are deleted (IP addresses stay). \fB\fBrecreate_required\fR\fP (422, invoiced products only): the target plan would need the service to be re-created on another platform, which deletes its data; the API never does that and nothing is changed or charged. Pick another plan from resize-options, or create a new server, move the data and delete the old one.

.PP
API: GET /cloud/services/{id}/resize-options (operationId getResizeOptions, scope services_read)


